# Rendering performance
@scenario tutorial_lesson_28
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: The wall hasn't moved and the light hasn't changed. Why shade the same picture again? Look at the cache on the second frame.
ginger: Run scripts/examples/window-light/scene.vns from the engine repository. Compare its first frame with repeated renders.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What makes a lighting cache safe to reuse?
> The previous image has the same filename alone. -> retry
> The source, rig and relevant dimensions still match. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The key has to represent the inputs that can change pixels. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: The key has to represent the inputs that can change pixels.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_28]
[flag tutorial_done_28]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
